{"schema":"metaphysica.path_patch/1","path":"theory_uncertainty_policy--always","files":{"geometry_to_physics.json":{"base_sha256":"80709c5cfc250d02775c49ca8c3aa851b9f3a1e05b803da97c35374a63085643","ops":[{"op":"replace","path":"/summary/by_tone/ok","value":28},{"op":"replace","path":"/summary/by_tone/fail","value":3},{"op":"replace","path":"/summary/by_verdict/PASS","value":8},{"op":"replace","path":"/summary/by_verdict/FAIL","value":3},{"op":"replace","path":"/summary/by_verdict/MARGINAL","value":3},{"op":"replace","path":"/steps/17/experiment/pull","value":1.003712508068823},{"op":"replace","path":"/steps/17/experiment/verdict","value":"MARGINAL"},{"op":"replace","path":"/steps/17/tone","value":"ok"},{"op":"replace","path":"/steps/18/experiment/pull","value":0.6842343525281191},{"op":"replace","path":"/steps/18/experiment/verdict","value":"PASS"},{"op":"replace","path":"/steps/18/tone","value":"ok"}]},"sections.json":{"base_sha256":"0875dba64a64e1cdfd037b13d85e25beee31abe2e949dd2357f5acdfc974a1bd","ops":[{"op":"replace","path":"/sections/0/contentBlocks/0/content","value":"<p>Principia Metaphysica is a speculative geometric model and has not been peer reviewed.</p><p><strong>Assumed.</strong> a 26D bulk of signature (24,2): 24 space directions and 2 times, one per shadow, split into two shadows. This is a postulate; nothing below derives it.</p><p><strong>Geometry.</strong> The internal space of each shadow is Y<sub>7</sub>, Joyce&rsquo;s resolution of T<sup>7</sup>/(&#8484;/2)<sup>3</sup>: a closed manifold with (b<sub>2</sub>, b<sub>3</sub>) = (12, 43) and n<sub>gen</sub> = b<sub>2</sub>/4 = 3, the number of singular involutions. A metric of holonomy exactly G<sub>2</sub> exists by Joyce 2000, Thm 11.6.1: 10 of 10 hypotheses are measured on the active seed and hold (closed by theorem). No explicit metric is claimed; none is known for any compact G<sub>2</sub> manifold.</p><p><strong>What follows.</strong> Read from the topology: the gauge content (CG.5), one K3 surface per singular involution (CG.9) and the effective index &chi;<sub>eff</sub> = 48n = 144 (the K3 reading; the Euler characteristic of Y<sub>7</sub> is 0). Two results are negative: holonomy exactly G<sub>2</sub> excludes the confining sector that racetrack stabilisation needs (CG.10), and the leading flux potential cannot accelerate the universe (CG.11).</p><p><strong>Against data.</strong> Scoreboard: 32 pass, 17 marginal, 11 tension and 18 fail, with chi-squared 2.24e+09 over 67 scored rows. The model does not fit the data globally. Chirality, moduli stabilisation, dark energy and flavour are open.</p>"},{"op":"replace","path":"/sections/0/content_blocks/0/content","value":"<p>Principia Metaphysica is a speculative geometric model and has not been peer reviewed.</p><p><strong>Assumed.</strong> a 26D bulk of signature (24,2): 24 space directions and 2 times, one per shadow, split into two shadows. This is a postulate; nothing below derives it.</p><p><strong>Geometry.</strong> The internal space of each shadow is Y<sub>7</sub>, Joyce&rsquo;s resolution of T<sup>7</sup>/(&#8484;/2)<sup>3</sup>: a closed manifold with (b<sub>2</sub>, b<sub>3</sub>) = (12, 43) and n<sub>gen</sub> = b<sub>2</sub>/4 = 3, the number of singular involutions. A metric of holonomy exactly G<sub>2</sub> exists by Joyce 2000, Thm 11.6.1: 10 of 10 hypotheses are measured on the active seed and hold (closed by theorem). No explicit metric is claimed; none is known for any compact G<sub>2</sub> manifold.</p><p><strong>What follows.</strong> Read from the topology: the gauge content (CG.5), one K3 surface per singular involution (CG.9) and the effective index &chi;<sub>eff</sub> = 48n = 144 (the K3 reading; the Euler characteristic of Y<sub>7</sub> is 0). Two results are negative: holonomy exactly G<sub>2</sub> excludes the confining sector that racetrack stabilisation needs (CG.10), and the leading flux potential cannot accelerate the universe (CG.11).</p><p><strong>Against data.</strong> 